mount - what is mounted where

SYNOPSIS
    mount

DESCRIPTION
    Lists the filesystems, read from /proc/mounts.

    It does not mount anything. There is one block filesystem here and no way
    to add a second yet - every superblock field in the server is a singleton
    - so an option to try would only ever fail.

    Three different things answer for parts of the tree: the ext4 filesystem
    on the disk, the /dev entries libc answers without asking anybody, and
    /proc, which is not storage at all.

SEE ALSO
    df, proc
